{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03680",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 4.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.54,
      "end_seconds": 11.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Alright, no problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.81,
      "end_seconds": 24.54,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "Um, so... a painful ulcer that is growing quickly. That's why I came. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.31,
      "end_seconds": 29.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.02,
      "end_seconds": 34.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Ah, I've had it for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.33,
      "end_seconds": 41.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.4,
      "end_seconds": 54.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "Mild, really. It happens a couple of times a week. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.8,
      "end_seconds": 60.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Has there been severe pain too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.95,
      "end_seconds": 66.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Let me think, yes, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.74,
      "end_seconds": 71.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.01,
      "end_seconds": 86.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.05,
      "end_seconds": 117.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 118 over 71, heart rate 78. And SpO2 98 percent on room air, respiratory rate 17, temperature is 36.9 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.52,
      "end_seconds": 124.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.56,
      "end_seconds": 126.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.7,
      "end_seconds": 149.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "The ulcer has a ragged purple edge with a boggy base and undermined borders."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.94,
      "end_seconds": 156.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.12,
      "end_seconds": 177.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Have you had fever, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.2,
      "end_seconds": 180.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.63,
      "end_seconds": 186.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "A few quick ones: recent injury, diabetes or recent cut?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.5,
      "end_seconds": 199.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Let me think, no recent injury, diabetes or recent cut, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.51,
      "end_seconds": 205.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.87,
      "end_seconds": 208.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "no, all normal there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.35,
      "end_seconds": 213.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "So, anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.51,
      "end_seconds": 220.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Actually, uh, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.54,
      "end_seconds": 240.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.46,
      "end_seconds": 246.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.78,
      "end_seconds": 250.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.45,
      "end_seconds": 256.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.76,
      "end_seconds": 261.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.83,
      "end_seconds": 264.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.98,
      "end_seconds": 268.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.04,
      "end_seconds": 271.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "no known allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.69,
      "end_seconds": 278.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.71,
      "end_seconds": 283.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Ah, no, I've always been fairly healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.36,
      "end_seconds": 299.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.85,
      "end_seconds": 304.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No, um, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.33,
      "end_seconds": 314.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards possible pyoderma gangrenosum linked to bowel inflammation. I can't rule out an infected ulcer yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.1,
      "end_seconds": 318.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.38,
      "end_seconds": 338.66,
      "duration_seconds": 19.28,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible pyoderma gangrenosum linked to bowel inflammation, and we'll know more once the a stool test is back. I want a stool test done, that's for bowel symptoms. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.02,
      "end_seconds": 341.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.24,
      "end_seconds": 353.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "do not cut or scrub it, that can make it worse. The dermatology clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.94,
      "end_seconds": 359.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Alright, you know, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.19,
      "end_seconds": 380.16,
      "duration_seconds": 19.97,
      "text": "Blood tests is something we might do if this doesn't improve in a month. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like to see you again after the biopsy. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.68,
      "end_seconds": 383.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Actually, alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}